# Bucket Isolation -- Three-Tier Model

RULE: Group A (raw data: instruments, market_data, features_calendar) has NO env in bucket name. Group B (derived data: features_*, ml_*, strategy, execution, pnl) ALWAYS uses get_bucket_environment() for mock/dev/prod isolation. Never hardcode bucket names in services. CLOUD_MOCK_MODE=true always routes Group B to mock tier.
WHY: Prevents dev/mock writes from polluting production buckets. Prod buckets are IAM write-protected.
CODEX: 05-infrastructure/bucket-isolation-model.md
SSOT: unified-cloud-interface/unified_cloud_interface/constants.py (get_bucket_environment, get_bucket_name, get_scenario_prefix)

DO:
  from unified_cloud_interface import get_bucket_name, get_bucket_environment, get_scenario_prefix
  bucket = get_bucket_name("strategy", "DEFI")  # auto-resolves mock/dev/prod
  prefix = get_scenario_prefix(scenario="stress")  # "scenario=stress/" in mock, "" in dev/prod

NEVER:
  bucket = f"strategy-store-defi-{project_id}"  # hardcoded, no env isolation
  bucket = f"strategy-store-defi-prod-{project_id}"  # hardcoded env
  Writing to prod buckets from CLOUD_MOCK_MODE=true or ENVIRONMENT=dev

## Data Catalogue
After every successful batch or live run, ManifestWriter writes a Parquet manifest to data-catalogue-{pid}/{service}/day={date}/manifest.parquet. This is automatic via ServiceCLI post-run hook.

## Data Status Feature Toggle
deployment-service data-status supports --source manifest|gcs|auto (env: DATA_STATUS_SOURCE, default: auto).
"auto" tries ManifestReader first (DuckDB over Parquet manifests), falls back to GCS blob scanning.
Use --source gcs for --check-venues/--check-data-types that need blob-level granularity.

## Scenario Routing (mock tier only)
--scenario flag routes reads/writes to scenario={name}/ subdirectory within mock buckets. Standard scenarios (default, stress, missing_data) are long-lived. Custom scenarios auto-expire after 30 days.
